    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d401">

                <pb facs="0391" n="321" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg321"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/2107: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d401-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic"> to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-02-02T13:00:00+01:00">February 2, 1934—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 2—8:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>226. A confidential letter from the Secretariat informs me that alarming reports
                    are current concerning military preparations by both <pb facs="0392" n="322"
                        xml:id="pg322"/> Colombia and Peru. The letter adds that the Committee of
                    Three set up by the Advisory Committee would be grateful to receive any
                    information as to the state of negotiations now being carried on at Rio de
                    Janeiro and as to prospects of the improvement in the relations between the two
                    countries. The Committee of Three has therefore requested the Secretariat to
                    make confidential inquiry of those Governments which are represented in Rio de
                    Janeiro, Lima and Bogotá as to whether they have any information which they
                    could put at the Committee’s disposal both now and during the next few
                    months.</p>
                <p>2. I am also informed that the Governments represented on the Committee of Three
                    (see telegram 225, January 18, 4 p.m., third paragraph<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d401-f2"/>) are already making inquiry in the three capitals
                    mentioned.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d401-f1" n="3" type="source" xml:id="d401-f1-content">
                <p>Hugh Robert Wilson, American representative on the advisory commission of the
                    League of Nations to observe developments in the Colombian-Peruvian dispute,
                    1933.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d401-f2" n="4" xml:id="d401-f2-content">
